## Changes
This PR adds a benchmark tool to measure how much time is some part of the code running for.

## How Has This Been Tested?
Jest.

## Examples
### Measure code execution time
Example from the CMS Create Entry GraphQL resolver:
```typescript
try {
    const entry = await context.benchmark.measure("headlessCms.createEntry", async () => {
        return context.cms.createEntry(model, args.data);
    });

    return new Response(entry);
} catch (e) {
    return new ErrorResponse(e);
}
```

### Enabling the benchmark
```typescript
new ContextPlugin(async context => {
    /**
     * Enabling benchmark when environment variable is set to "true".
     */
    context.benchmark.enableOn(async () => {
        return process.env.BENCHMARK_ENABLE === "true";
    });
    /**
     * Enabling benchmark when "x-benchmark" header is set to "true".
     */
    context.benchmark.enableOn(async () => {
        return context.request.headers["x-benchmark"] === "true";
    });
});
```

### Outputting the results to another system
```typescript
new ContextPlugin(async context => {
    context.benchmark.onOutput(async benchmark => {
        await sendToOutsideSystem(benchmark.measurements);

        return BenchmarkOutputCallableResponse.BREAK;
    });
});
```

